1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:02,312
First, a confession.

2
00:00:02,332 --> 00:00:03,082
Right now,

3
00:00:03,102 --> 00:00:04,024
you are moving.

4
00:00:04,044 --> 00:00:05,148
Fast.

5
00:00:05,168 --> 00:00:06,938
Earth spins once a day,

6
00:00:06,958 --> 00:00:07,938
and at the equator,

7
00:00:07,958 --> 00:00:09,322
the ground beneath you travels

8
00:00:09,322 --> 00:00:11,713
about 1,670 kilometers per hour.

9
00:00:13,063 --> 00:00:13,986
The farther you are from

10
00:00:13,986 --> 00:00:14,853
the equator,

11
00:00:14,873 --> 00:00:15,877
the slower you go.

12
00:00:15,897 --> 00:00:19,535
New York cruises at about 1,270.

13
00:00:19,555 --> 00:00:22,197
London, about 1,040.

14
00:00:22,217 --> 00:00:23,467
At the North Pole,

15
00:00:23,487 --> 00:00:24,456
you're just turning in a

16
00:00:24,456 --> 00:00:25,195
very slow circle.

17
00:00:26,195 --> 00:00:27,532
And that's just the spin.

18
00:00:27,552 --> 00:00:28,896
Earth also races around the

19
00:00:28,896 --> 00:00:30,727
Sun at about 107,000

20
00:00:30,727 --> 00:00:32,082
kilometers per hour,

21
00:00:32,102 --> 00:00:33,267
while the Sun drags us

22
00:00:33,267 --> 00:00:35,426
around the galaxy even faster.

23
00:00:35,446 --> 00:00:38,130
Relax: nobody is stopping those.

24
00:00:38,150 --> 00:00:38,599
Today.

25
00:00:39,949 --> 00:00:41,232
So why don't you feel it?

26
00:00:41,252 --> 00:00:42,266
Because everything moves with

27
00:00:42,266 --> 00:00:43,462
you: the ground,

28
00:00:43,482 --> 00:00:44,585
the air, the oceans.

29
00:00:44,605 --> 00:00:45,928
It's like a smooth flight.

30
00:00:45,948 --> 00:00:46,943
You can sip coffee at

31
00:00:46,943 --> 00:00:49,420
900 km/h without spilling a drop.
